<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Older bungalows, cement stucco and newer infills</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>Calgary Parging said in 2024 that cement stucco with an acrylic finish is its main product on over 87% of the residential properties it works on, though that is its own job mix and not a city count. A traditional three-coat system, as specified by Imasco, has a scratch coat of at least 10 mm (3/8 inch) and a brown coat that brings the combined system to 19 mm.</p><p>Some walls carry a different system, such as EIFS, and the repair method changes with it. Calgary Parging reports that woodpeckers go after EIFS because the foam behind the finish is softer than concrete and sounds hollow when tapped. The contractor who visits can tell you which system your wall is. Our page on <a href="/stucco-repair-calgary/">stucco repair in Calgary</a> explains how a visit and quote work.</p><p>Age matters too. Across the city, 26% of occupied dwellings date from 1961 to 1980 and 12% from 1981 to 1990 (2021 figures), so older homes are common well beyond the southwest. In Signal Hill, a West-sector community, 62% of dwellings were built 1991 to 2000. Imasco notes that some cracking and efflorescence are inherent to portland cement, so not every crack means a failed wall.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Chinooks, freeze-thaw and snow against the wall</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>The weather figures here are city-wide, but they are what southwest walls go through too. In 2022 Calgary recorded 117 freeze-thaw cycles (the 30-year average is 128) and 54 chinook days (average 46). The City of Calgary says stucco does not handle moisture well, and that moisture and snow can cause it to shrink and crack.</p><p>Martini Stone Masonry, a Calgary contractor, reports that snow piled against stucco softens and crumbles the lowest 12 to 18 inches of the wall, and that temperature movement opens gaps of 3 to 8 mm where stucco meets frames. Calgary Parging says over 30% of its residential repairs address water damage from incorrectly installed rain gutters, eaves or flashing. Where your downspouts discharge and where snow piles up are worth a look before the visit.</p><p>Timing matters as well. Imasco's guidance is no stucco work when air and substrate temperatures are below 4°C for 24 hours before, during and after application, and Calgary Parging says off-season repairs need heated hoarding. Winter is a sensible time to document damage and collect quotes; ask each contractor what they can do in cold weather and how. See <a href="/stucco-repair-cost-calgary/">stucco repair cost in Calgary</a> for published price examples.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Hail, woodpeckers and insurance in the southwest</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>The City of Calgary says all communities in the city are equally exposed to hail, so no corner of the southwest is safe or riskier by default. It also says stucco holds up well to flying debris in moderate wind and hail, but severe storms can cause damage. If you think hail has marked your walls, photograph the damage and call your insurer first. The City advises contacting your home insurance provider before any repair work. A contractor can then give you a written repair estimate to pass along. More detail is on our <a href="/hail-woodpecker-stucco-damage/">hail and woodpecker damage</a> page.</p><p>Northern flickers are protected under the federal Migratory Birds Convention Act. Calgary Parging says flickers work Calgary stucco hard, especially on west and south elevations in spring. An empty hole with no live bird or viable egg may be repaired without a permit; if a bird is using it, wait until nesting ends. Environment and Climate Change Canada says access can be cut off with a tarp or wire mesh.</p><p>Before you sign anything, get written quotes from more than one business and confirm the contractor's City of Calgary business licence by calling 311. A contractor who takes money before finishing the work and solicits the contract in person away from its own premises needs an Alberta prepaid contracting licence, which you can check with Service Alberta. This page is advertising paid by contractors; the site does not file, manage or negotiate insurance claims.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#F3ECE1;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">What does stucco repair cost in Southwest Calgary?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">No price is published for Southwest Calgary specifically. As examples, Calgary Parging lists small patch repairs at $550 to $1,125 and medium repairs of two or three areas at $1,250 to $2,650, both before GST. Other Calgary firms publish different figures on their own pages. The contractor who sees your wall sets the actual quote.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">Is the stucco on my Southwest Calgary bungalow the same as on a newer infill?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Not necessarily. Calgary Parging says cement stucco with an acrylic finish covers over 87% of the homes it works on, but some walls are EIFS, which is repaired differently. Ask the contractor to identify the system before quoting, and make sure the materials and work are written into the contract.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">Can stucco be repaired in winter in Southwest Calgary?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Guidance from suppliers is cautious. Imasco says no stucco work below 4°C in air and substrate for 24 hours before, during and after application, and Calgary Parging says stucco cures best above 5°C in dry conditions, typically April through October. Winter is a good time to have damage assessed and quoted. Ask any contractor who offers cold-weather work how they protect the wall.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">I have hail damage on my Southwest Calgary home. Can Sandstone Stucco Co help with the claim?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">No. This site is advertising and does not file, manage or negotiate insurance claims. Call your insurer first, take photos and keep your receipts, as the Insurance Bureau of Canada advises. A contractor can give you a written repair estimate you may pass to your insurer, and whether hail damage is covered depends on your own policy.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
